props:
Use case: stylized-concept.
Asset type: transparent game prop atlas, 4 columns x 3 rows, twelve 512x512 cells on a 2048x1536 canvas.
Match the detailed painted and inked side-view storybook environment in the reference. Halloween in a burned forest, gray ash, muted violet stone, amber lantern light, teal-violet ghost vapor. Objects only, absolutely no characters or lettering. Every object has a clean transparent exterior, no backdrop rectangles. Natural grounded bases.
Cells in READING order:
1: one tall blackened leafless tree with spreading gnarled roots;
2: a low group of two charred broken stumps and ash;
3: three crooked old gravestones and dry vines;
4: two beautiful carved pumpkin lanterns with warm golden faces, low dead leaves;
5: one closed grave: rounded tombstone centered at x=256 and an intact stone slab on dark soil, front three-quarter view;
6: THE SAME grave, same tombstone and soil positions, slab cracked with tiny purple light seeping out;
7: THE SAME grave, slab partly pushed apart with a painted curling violet smoky cloud rising;
8: THE SAME grave now open, a small deep-black opening following the slab outline and fading ghost smoke. No zombie built into it;
9: a closed wrought-iron cemetery gateway with two worn stone posts and low dry vines;
10: THE SAME gateway opened, doors hinged outward, same posts and footprint; transparent passage;
11: a second cluster of small leaning gravestones and one low broken fence;
12: one small distant crooked village house with warm windows, ash-dark roof, subtle Halloween decoration.
Keep each cell separate with generous gutters. Grave animation cells 5-8 must keep exact tombstone/slab scale, camera and ground baseline, changing only the slab and smoke. Gateway cells 9-10 must keep exact post positions, scale and camera. No side tilting of the whole object, no opaque checkerboard, no SVG, no UI, no perspective change between animation frames.
